+	// Huawei VRP VMs (CE12800 switch, NE40E router). PLATFORM-SPECIFIC, patch 0085.
+	//
+	// Three measured facts shape this profile (2026-11-19, V200R005C10 CE12800 and
+	// V800R011C00 NE40E on node-a):
+	//  1. SSH never reached VRP over a plain virtio NIC: the host hands the guest TCP
+	//     segments CHECKSUM_PARTIAL and VRP's TCP stack drops them (tcpdump on tap0 shows
+	//     the SYN with an incomplete checksum; `display tcp statistics` stays 0 while the
+	//     interface Input counter rises). `ethtool -K tap0 tx off` fixes it, and so does
+	//     the libvirt <driver><guest csum='off' .../> setting the hook below applies.
+	//     e1000 is NOT an alternative: the guest never transmits on it.
+	//  2. NIC index 1 (the first NIC after the masquerade management NIC) is a
+	//     placeholder VRP never maps to a port (vrnetlab's "required dummy"). The first
+	//     data port (CE GE1/0/0, NE Ethernet1/0/0) is NIC index 2. See
+	//     kubeVirtHuaweiNICSlots.
+	//  3. q35 + host-passthrough + virtio on every NIC boots both images.
